lesson.body:
If dividend is not paid within 30 days of declaration:

- every director who is knowingly a party to the default is punishable with imprisonment up to 2 years and a fine of at least ₹1,000 for every day of default;
- the company pays simple interest at 18% per annum for the period of default.

No offence is committed where the dividend could not be paid:

- by operation of law;
- because the shareholder's directions about payment could not be complied with and this was communicated to him;
- because of a dispute about the right to receive it;
- because it was lawfully adjusted by the company against a sum due from the shareholder;
- for any other reason not due to default on the part of the company.

Section 126: where a transfer of shares has not been registered, the dividend on those shares is transferred to the Unpaid Dividend Account unless the registered holder authorises payment to the transferee.

**Common mistakes**: using revaluation reserve or unrealised fair-value gains for dividend; forgetting that the drawn amount first covers the current-year loss; confusing the 5-day bank deposit with the 30-day payment period.

